      "body": "Adds a guided payment playground, shared service contracts, bounded structured extraction and a local agent kit with explicit call/session spending limits.\n\nOpt-in receipt recovery now saves successful results before settlement and uses atomic Redis claims to prevent duplicate authorization execution. A secret client-generated receipt capability permits retrieval without submitting another payment. Results last 24 hours (128 KiB cap); authorization metadata/tombstones last seven days. Pending settlement can be reconciled from a known transaction only after 12 confirmations and matching USDC authorization/transfer events. Recovery supports exact EIP-3009 USDC on Base/Base Sepolia. The agent kit has six MCP tools, including recovery that never signs again, leaks bearer capabilities or resets spending. /developers#receipts, OpenAPI and RECEIPTS.md document setup and limitations.\n\nValidation: type checks, unit and reliability checks, five contract tests, ten receipt tests and 18 agent-kit tests passed. Receipt tests use the actual installed Next x402 wrapper with a mock facilitator and cover storage failure before/after settlement and dropped settlement responses. Production build passed; existing viem/ox dynamic import warning remains. Local developer page, no-store receipt availability, unauthorized retrieval and OpenAPI reference were checked. Uploaded GitHub tree matches the tested local tree exactly.\n\nPreview: https://vending-machine-git-feat-x402-reliability-playground-x-vendor.vercel.app/developers#receipts\n\nRelease gate: funded E2E on portalv2 and real Redis persistence/atomicity/failover validation remain pending. Receipt storage uses existing configured Redis credentials; it fails closed when unavailable. If a transaction hash is lost, operator reconciliation is still needed; automatic chain-history scanning is not implemented. External LLM evaluation prompts are provided without a claimed score.\n\nRemaining roadmap: domain health/SPF/DMARC, Kronos evaluation, remaining branding and dependency work. Branch audit is recorded in PLAN.md; nothing deleted or merged. Draft against master; production unchanged.",
