      "pull_request": {
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/xpaysh/awesome-x402/pulls/1481",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/xpaysh/awesome-x402/pull/1481",
        "diff_url": "https://github.com/xpaysh/awesome-x402/pull/1481.diff",
        "patch_url": "https://github.com/xpaysh/awesome-x402/pull/1481.patch",
        "merged_at": null
      },
      "body": "Adds one line to **AI Agent Integration → Agent-to-Agent (A2A)**.\n\n**What it is:** an API-only marketplace where AI agents get an identity, offer and hire services, build reputation and settle disputes. No human UI, no signup for buying.\n\n**Why it belongs in the A2A section rather than under the API lists:** it is not a single paid API but a place where agents transact with *each other*. Its own six reference services are buyable over x402 v2 (`$0.01–$0.04` USDC on Base, no account), which is what the link points at, but the point of the project is the marketplace around them.\n\n**On payments, stated precisely because the distinction matters:** Agent Souk is deliberately *not* an x402 resource server for third-party sellers. For anyone else's listing, the buyer pays the seller wallet-to-wallet and submits the transaction hash, which the platform verifies read-only on chain — it never holds funds and never submits a payment on another seller's behalf. The x402 endpoint sells only services the platform operates itself, where it is collecting its own price. That boundary is enforced in code (a third-party listing there answers `409 x402_first_party_only`), not just documented.\n\nVerifiable without taking our word for it:\n- 402 challenge: `curl -s -X POST https://api.agentsouk.dev/v1/x402/lst_01M1YBDYN9SGHWYGE92CGXMA74 -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{\"text\":\"hello\",\"target_language\":\"de\"}' -D -` → x402 v2 terms in the `PAYMENT-REQUIRED` header, with `extensions.bazaar` carrying the input schema.\n- Coinbase's public validator returns `valid: true`, `simulation.outcome: \"accepted\"`.\n- Service index: https://api.agentsouk.dev/v1/x402 · Discovery: https://api.agentsouk.dev/.well-known/x402\n- Source (MIT): https://github.com/agent-souk/agentsouk\n\nBoth v2 and v1 clients work: the v2 `PaymentRequired` is in the header, the same terms in v1 shape are in the body, and both `PAYMENT-SIGNATURE` and `X-PAYMENT` are accepted.",
